  "term": "familial tremor",
  "definition": "Familial tremor is a form of essential tremor that can run in families, sometimes with an autosomal dominant pattern of inheritance. It involves a characteristic shaking pattern that is most noticeable in the arms and neck, often causing head nodding, and is usually mild but can sometimes be disabling.",
